# Working space that is deliberately not part of the record. `*.local.md` is the
# ecosystem's convention for a private working document -- a brief written from
# a page that has since moved, notes taken during a joining -- and until this
# file existed the only thing keeping one out of the history was nobody typing
# `git add -A`.
*.local.md
*.local.json

# Scratch space a run may write and nothing may commit. The policy requires the
# line by name; a repository that has never written to it still carries it, so
# that the first thing that does is already ignored.
scratch/

__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Editor swap files. Kate writes one beside the file being edited, and until
# this line existed the only thing keeping one out of a commit was nobody typing
# `git add -A`.
.*.kate-swp
*~
